# MIME types served by the site — the vault mime lane (the wave D growth).
# Generated programmatically from the known extension corpus: the live IANA
# media types registry (2026-10-30 snapshot), the node mime-db, the apache httpd
# mime.types, the nginx mime.types, the apache tika catalog, the rust mime_guess
# table (the MimeTypeMap corpus), the go builtin table and the family catalog of
# the argan gateway — with the family law rows pinned: .ts answers video/mp2t,
# .tsx answers application/typescript.
# The line order is the collision law: the family groups run application, video,
# audio, image, font, model, chemical, message, multipart, text, then the legacy
# trees alphabetical — the first row claiming an extension keeps it, exactly the
# way the serving index answers a lookup.
